{"tool_name":"3d-dart","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"3d-dart","home":"https://milou.science.uu.nl/services/3DDART/","summary":"A web server for generation of 3D-structural DNA models with a defined conformation by providing control over both \u2018global\u2019 and \u2018local\u2019 conformational features.","addition_date":"2015-03-05T10:30:40Z","last_update_date":"2026-04-19T09:24:16.551817Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1"],"collections":["EGI","EOSC-Hub","INSTRUCT","WeNMR"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:3d-dart","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"a.m.j.j.bonvin@uu.nl","name":"Bonvin Lab","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7369-1322","typeEntity":"Division","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer","Primary contact","Provider"],"url":"http://www.bonvinlab.org"},{"name":"Utrecht University","url":"http://www.uu.nl"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://milou.science.uu.nl/services/3DDART/DARTusage.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-EE","a.m.j.j.bonvin@uu.nl","esraa9"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"note":"3DNA driven - DNA Analysis and Rebuilding Tools. Provides a means of analyzing nucleic acid structures and generating custom models.","operation":[{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2476"},{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2481"},{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"3D-DART","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"esraa9","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkp287","metadata":{"abstract":"There is a growing interest in structural studies of DNA by both experimental and computational approaches. Often, 3D-structural models of DNA are required, for instance, to serve as templates for homology modeling, as starting structures for macro-molecular docking or as scaffold for NMR structure calculations. The conformational adaptability of DNA when binding to a protein is often an important factor and at the same time a limitation in such studies. As a response to the demand for 3D-structural models reflecting the intrinsic plasticity of DNA we present the 3D-DART server (3D NA-Driven D NA A nalysis and R ebuilding T ool). The server provides an easy interface to a powerful collection of tools for the generation of DNA-structural models in custom conformations. The computational engine beyond the server makes use of the 3DNA software suite together with a collection of home-written python scripts. The server is freely available at http://haddock.chem.uu.nl/dna without any login requirement.","authors":[{"name":"Bonvin A.M.J.J."},{"name":"van Dijk M."}],"citationCount":279,"date":"2009-08-04T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"3D-DART: A DNA structure modelling server"},"pmcid":"PMC2703913","pmid":"19417072","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0092"},{"term":"NMR","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0593"},{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0097"},{"term":"Structural biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_1317"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"3D-DART","home":"https://bio.tools/3d-dart","version":"1","summary":"A web server for generation of 3D-structural DNA models with a defined conformation by providing control over both \u2018global\u2019 and \u2018local\u2019 conformational features.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:3d-dart:1/web/milou.science.uu.nl","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":150,"citations":[{"count":3,"year":"2010"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count"